cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FlowMLLab, please cite the v1.4.0 software release and the associated article."
title: "FlowMLLab: An Open-Source Framework for Reproducible CFD-to-Scientific-Machine-Learning Experiments"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Roohi
    given-names: Ehsan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5739-3210"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ehsan-Roohi/FlowMLLab"
url: "https://github.com/Ehsan-Roohi/FlowMLLab/releases/tag/v1.4.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  FlowMLLab integrates transparent continuum and particle solvers, case-wise
  data partitions, non-neural baselines, coordinate networks, POD-DeepONet,
  centered POD-Galerkin and POD-DEIM models, a D2Q9 lattice-Boltzmann
  cylinder-wake module, exact and learned gas-dynamics inverse benchmarks,
  physical diagnostics,
  machine-readable validation evidence, and release-quality assurance for
  reproducible scientific machine learning in fluid mechanics.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - scientific machine learning
  - neural operators
  - proper orthogonal decomposition
  - discrete empirical interpolation method
  - lattice Boltzmann method
  - cylinder wake
  - gas dynamics
  - compressible flow
  - direct simulation Monte Carlo
  - reproducibility
version: "1.4.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22315623"
date-released: "2026-09-04"
